{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788977998,"nonce":"iQrM9UBJwF7NElZhMGXbLTus/jI=","message":"Fixed in 8b99c44.\n\ncall_compiled_function has exactly three failure paths: an arity the fixed ladder cannot marshal, raised before control reaches compiled code; a Haxe throw; and a longjmp arriving with no exception recorded. Only the first is safe to retry.\n\nThe caller retried everything except the throw, so the longjmp-without-exception case still re-entered a body that may already have allocated, mutated a field or written output. CompiledEntryRefused now tags the pre-entry refusal and only that arm falls through to execute_hl_function; every other error propagates. The safe direction is the default rather than the exception.\n\nThe compiled-only path was already correct -- it has no fallback by design.\n\nFull suite green.","files":null}]}